    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.3,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.99,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stay flat at about 0.90–0.95 from 6 h to 18 h, after roughly doubling every hour up to 5 h. That flat line looks like the reader saturating rather than growth stopping. I diluted the 18 h aliquot and got 0.334 at 10-fold (mean of 3 replicates: 0.323, 0.334, 0.346) and 0.0815 at 40-fold (1 replicate). Scaled back up, these give about 3.34 and 3.26. The two dilutions agree, so the signal is linear in that range. The true 18 h OD is therefore about 3.3, roughly 3.6 times the undiluted reading of 0.91, so the undiluted readings underestimate the biomass."
  },
